WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.380
"Ah, our lord and liege. Twas the soul of my sister."

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.080
Of the three sisters who founded the sable church,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.040
Elfriede was the eldest and their leader.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:20.360
Together, with the hollows of Londor, they fought to usurp the first flame for Hollow kind.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.220
And you, of course, were a part of that in one of the endings.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:32.140
But before you came along, it appears that there was another who tried to usurp the flame, but failed.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:40.000
"Alfriede, a poor wench turned to ash, who would abandon Londor."

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:46.200
Unkindled ash, in Miyazaki's own words, are Undead who failed to link the flame.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:55.200
And in the opening cutscene I personally think that we see the soul of cinder dragging and cremating one of those failures.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.000
One of those undead that failed to take him on and turned into ash.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.420
And these are failures that can rise again when the link of fire is threatened.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.200
Failures like Elfriede. Failures like you.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.040
After her failure, Elfriede truly distanced herself from the church.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.300
Don't forget- we know that you need to be very forlorn to find this painted world.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.300
So it's possible that she found this place in her despair.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.260
And when she arrived she didn't sit meekly by like so many other creatures in this place.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:35.680
No, instead she decided that this was a world and a people that she wished to protect.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:42.760
For this world really is a reflection of the outside and, as a result,

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.240
it was a chance for her to take a truly different path.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:54.420
On the outside, the fire fades and a great sacrifice triggers the rebirth of this world.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.480
And on the inside in the painting, the painting falls to rot.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.960
And it's residents set it aflame to put an end to the rot.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.080
Painting a new world for themselves just after this happens.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.300
Both places have a cycle of rebirth and on the outside

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:16.580
Elfriede died attempting to break that cycle and usurp the flame.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.820
And after her failure she fights for the exact opposite fate within the painting.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:26.420
She renounced everything and she fights to keep things the way they are now.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.680
To embrace the rot, the stagnation, the stasis.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.240
To force her version of kindness upon the residents of the painting.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.700
"How this came to pass, I know not."

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:43.900
"But take heed: kindness can wear upon one's principles."

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.760
And beyond the gate, which looks like it was broken inwards

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:54.520
as if someone forced their way in, is father Ariandel, restorer of the painted world.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.200
Or what's become of him, anyway.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.660
"I see flame. Flame, fluttering once again."

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.400
"Not enough blood yet shed."

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:12.660
"My flail. Bring me my flail."

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.840
The birdlike corvians refer to him fondly as "the good Father" which belies

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.500
a close relationship between the two of them.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:26.560
I have a feeling they don't think he can do any wrong, because they say this:

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:36.300
"But that witch fooled the good father and buried the flame. After we had all made up our minds, too."

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.820
That witch 'fooled' the good father. On the other hand,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:46.720
Friede's soul says that, together, with the good Father, they chose rot over flame.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:54.160
So did Ariandel betray the world he painted? Or was he bewitched as the corvians would like to believe.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.100
And so began this terrible partnership.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:05.160
Friede watches over the Father who, strapped to his chair, flails himself to produce blood to protect their secret.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.420
And the secret is the flame that they buried.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.540
After all, Ariandel knew that their world was painted with blood.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.080
And he knew that only blood could appease the flame.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.580
It's rather the same on the outside as well.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.260
Ours is the blood that keeps the fire alive.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.960
It's our sacrifice, and I think they're trying to make a point here about that.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.820
Just outside, Friede sits. Waiting, guarding.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:36.060
"Lord of hollows. I know not the missteps which led thee to this painted world.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.220
"But thy duty is all. And thy duty lieth elsewhere."

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:47.700
"Sweep all thought of us from thy mind. As thy kind always have."

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:53.060
It is said that when the ashes are two the flame will alight.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.200
So Friede and Wilhelm: they want you gone.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:01.320
Because they're hopeful that they can avoid conflict between the two ashes.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:07.120
For conflict could easily prove their prophecy right and rouse the withering flame.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.240
Wilhelm stands further out, and he's likely

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.980
the person that Yuria says stood by Elfriede until the end,

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.780
in the shadows cast by fire.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:23.580
"You look to be unkindled. No bell tolls, and yet you've slipped into the painting."

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.320
In the outside, the Firelink bell tolls when the link of fire is threatened

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.520
and it awakens the unkindled from their graves.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.800
Here, too, it seems that a bell is supposed to draw unkindled into the painting.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.540
Or it would, if it wasn't buried in the snow here.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.500
I'd say that Wilhelm and Elfriede have something to do with it.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:53.180
"You're Lady Yuria's Lord of Hollows. Lady Friede has spoken, has she not?"

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:59.140
"Then tarry no longer and begone. Carry on, for Lady Yuria and for Londor."

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:06.960
So Wilhelm, renowned as a cold blooded hangman, once served the three sisters of the Sable Church.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.120
He was, however, particularly loyal to the eldest.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.840
And yet, the time came when Elfriede bode him farewell.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:23.100
She gave him the onyx blade, this black, twisted sword that could enwreathe itself with black flame.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.300
Which is the flame that smolders within Elfriede.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.760
It is a weapon that is very personal to her and this gift says a lot.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.540
Most curiously though, the item description says that this sword was

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:42.760
a farewell gift, the acceptance of which signified Wilhelm's resignation from Elfriede's service.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:49.080
And that's weird because in the painting it seems as if he's still in her service, right?

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:55.360
So I take this line to mean that he was relieved of service to Elfriede's Sable Church

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.060
not to Elfriede in particular.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:01.800
But even after she failed to usurp the flame

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.980
if that is indeed what happened

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.020
he remains loyal.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.920
So loyal, that even Yuria asks us to remember his name.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.520
So loyal, that he would guard the white-haired woman with his life

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.780
and defend her against all intruders.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:21.560
"I've seen your kind. Time and time again."

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:28.120
"Every fleeing man must be caught. Every secret must be unearthed."

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.460
"Such is the conceit of the self-proclaimed seeker of truth."

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:38.540
"But in the end, you lack the stomach for the agony that you'll bring upon yourself."

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.060
Let's talk about Friede's boss fight.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:48.480
The boss fights in Souls that feature resurrection: I reckon they're the most fitting in the series

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.260
since our character has that ability to come back and kill them

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.900
multiple times, so why can't they do that, too?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.420
Lorian and Lothric, the Abyss Watchers, and now, Friede,

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.300
who is resurrected twice by the fire.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.940
And the second time, when the father falls, he utters:

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:12.220
"When the ashes are two, a flame alighteth".

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.260
Notice, this line is in quotation marks.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:22.800
As he appears to be quoting the tale that everyone in this painting repeats multiple times.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:26.260
"When the ashes are two, a flame alighteth".

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.560
And, as Friede is resurrected by the flame:

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:34.700
"Thou'rt Ash, and fire befits thee, of course".

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.760
I think, and maybe this is obvious, but

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:44.780
I think that Father Ariandel interprets this tale or prophecy

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:48.220
as meaning: "when the ashes are two, the black flame

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.020
within Friede shows itself".

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.060
Because he'd much rather interpret it that way than the alternative

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:59.940
which is to say that he'd rather Friede alight than his world be set aflame.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:04.280
Of course, Friede really is destined to fall to us in the end.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.860
And that's it.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.680
We've met two founders of the Sable Church now.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:14.340
We've met Elfriede, the eldest, who lost herself in the painting.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.940
We've met Yuria, in search of her true lord of hollows.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.100
And we've yet to meet the youngest sister, Lillian.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.500
Assumedly this could be her, in the final cutscene, right?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.860
Do you reckon we'll go to Londor?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.600
It seems logical because the usurping of the fire, that ending,

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.300
is one of the rare times an ending has felt like the series is progressing.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:41.940
And, with most of our questions related to the nature of hollowing and the origins of the undead curse,

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.060
I could really see Londor holding some answers

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:48.520
but I've definitely been wrong in my DLC predictions before so

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:53.500
let's just wait and see. I'm going to be a bit more conservative with some of my assumptions.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.540
So, I'll see you next time. Merry Christmas, guys.

